(III) (च्)--a northern kingdom and tribe whose king contemporary of कृष्ण was शकुनि who was an ally of जरासन्ध. Hence his subjects were enlisted by जरासन्ध against the Yadus. शकुनि himself was placed on the east of Gomanta hill during its siege. Here Bharata's sons तक्ष and पुष्कर ruled;
